ential gynaecological aetiology)", "Significant alcohol use (5+ drinks daily) as a Tier 5 risk factor", "Recent rapid weight loss for a fitness competition"], "excluded_candidates": ["Pelvic inflammatory disease: Lower abdominal pain pattern mismatch", "Ectopic pregnancy: Oral contraceptive use reduces likelihood but doesn't exclude possibility", "Alcoholic hepatitis: Chronic pattern discrepancy", "Acute pancreatitis: Epigastric pain pattern discrepancy", "Exercise-induced rhabdomyolysis: Possible but lacks direct evidence", "Hepatic flexure injury: No trauma history to support"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with compensatory tachycardia", "Acute haemodynamic instability requiring fluid resuscitation", "Potential for ruptured ectopic pregnancy (β-hCG pending)", "Risk of septic shock from undiagnosed intra-abdominal infection"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic Emergency (e.g., ectopic pregnancy, ovarian torsion)", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.089, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Chronic alcohol use and weight loss moderately reduce likelihood of ectopic pregnancy. Net effect is moderate_against."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Emergency (e.g., Budd-Chiari syndrome)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.21875, "posterior": 0.31683168316831684, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of pleuritic chest pain and athletic build weakly discounts Budd-Chiari syndrome. Net effect is weak_against."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction (e.g., choledocholithiasis)", "parent": 